The '''Bight of Ayorin Crisis''', sometimes called the '''Ayori-Sanyanian War''', was a short-lived conflict between [[Ayorin]] and [[Sanyan]] in the [[Bight of Ayorin]]. The war, which took place in November 1976, saw Ayorin unsuccessfully attempt to curtail Sanyanian oil-drilling and shipping interests in the Bight. Most of the fighting took place in small-scale sea and air engagements until the conflict was halted through mediation by [[Burawa]]. The subsequent [[Kankadaka Agreement]] delineated clear economic boundaries in the maritime oil-drilling regions.

The Crisis occurred against the backdrop of the [[Camboriú War]] and was timed by Ayori war planners to coincide with Sanyan's ally [[Balisca]] being engaged in [[Potocsí]] and unable to commit additional forces to the conflict in Kaftia.

